      "writtenOn": "2017-07-10T03:52:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When is this object garbage collected? Is it guaranteed that it is never garbage collected for as long as nai exists, and can be garbage collected after it stops existing?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4540,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 4540,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "c137a489bd7819b3c85de0a4bccffdb3236918f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e4bd4a7_430d47ed",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4540,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-24T13:39:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The service registering this anonymous instance necessarily needs to keep a pointer until it gets unregistered. So GC cannot happen sooner than unregistration.\n\nAlso, if this object is alive, then nai is alive because the GC cannot legally collect nai.\n\nThis objects stops being alive when it unregisters itself with interfaceRemoved.\n\nI am not sure that I understand the reason of your question. What are you trying to point out more specifically ?",
      "parentUuid": "dc162c50_7eb0af9b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4540,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 4540,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "c137a489bd7819b3c85de0a4bccffdb3236918f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e472618d_67b5191d",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4569,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-10T03:52:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we move this code to Nat464Xlat.java?\n\nEvery Nat464Xlat object already has access to the ConnectivityService handler and NetworkManagementService reference.\n\nPersonally I don\u0027t think this belongs in ConnectivityService, and even if it does, CS is so large that it\u0027s a good idea to move code to other files instead of keeping it all here. Existing examples are PacketKeepaliveTracker and NetworkAgentInfo, both of which contain code that runs inline on the ConnectivityService handler thread.\n\nPutting it in Nat464Xlat also has the advantage that it will be able to access instance fields such as mIface and mBaseIface, if it needs to.\n\nI think it could also simplify this code by removing some null guards.\n\nAlso, I think it would improve readability because it would encapsulate most of the 464xlat state management and lifecycle in one file.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4539,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4569,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c137a489bd7819b3c85de0a4bccffdb3236918f9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
